@startuml
title RPRRSBSI-V4 Input Workflow and Calculation Dependency Graphs
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 10
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #F0F4FF
  BorderColor #3366CC
}

package "Input workflow graph: what to ask next" #FFF5E6 {
  component "InputWorkflowNode\n(question/group/branch)" as Node
  component "InputWorkflowEdge" as Edge
  component "InputWorkflowCondition" as Condition
  component "RuleInputDefinition" as InputDefinition
  Node --> Edge
  Edge --> Node : next
  Edge --> Condition : guarded by
  Node --> InputDefinition : collects
}

package "Calculation graph: what to recompute" #EEF6EE {
  component "RuleVariant" as Variant
  component "RuleDependencyEdge" as Dependency
  component "RuleOutputDefinition" as Output
  component "RuleOutputInputBinding" as Binding
  component "DirtyWorkItem" as Dirty
  component "ExecutionAttempt" as Attempt
  component "ExecutionResult" as Result
  Variant --> Output : declares
  Variant --> Dependency : depends on
  Dependency --> Variant : prerequisite
  Output --> Binding : supplies
  Binding --> InputDefinition : maps into
  Dependency --> Dirty : invalidation creates
  Dirty --> Attempt : schedules
  Attempt --> Result : produces
}

note bottom of Condition
  Workflow cycles are permitted only when explicitly
  bounded and validated. Calculation cycles are rejected.
end note
note bottom of Dirty
  A changed input dirties the smallest reachable
  calculation subgraph, not the entire expert system.
end note
note bottom of InputDefinition
  D-3 RATIFIED:
  a material declared-type change creates a new
  semantic identity; meaning is not mutated in place.
  The eight documented edge cases remain
  HITL-PENDING and explicitly unclassified.
end note

note top of Attempt
  V4-2 scheduled ContentSummary ingestion uses
  the same explicit attempt, checkpoint, idempotency,
  and provenance principles, but remains a separate
  host-service workflow from the calculation DAG.
end note
@enduml
